<%# locals: title (String), heading_id (String, optional — set it when something
    inside the card points at the heading with aria-labelledby), attributes (Hash
    of extra section attributes, optional — the profit chart mounts its Stimulus
    controller on the card itself), note (String, optional — a caveat that
    belongs with the panel, under its heading, rather than in a help page).

    The card chrome — white panel, hairline border, small heading — shared by
    every panel on the analysis and category screens. It was written out four
    times before this partial existed, which is how a card style starts to drift.
    Rendered as a layout, so each caller supplies its own body. %>
<section class="card" <%= tag.attributes(local_assigns.fetch(:attributes, {})) %>>
  <%= tag.h2 title, id: local_assigns[:heading_id], class: "font-medium text-sm mb-3 text-text" %>
  <% if local_assigns[:note].present? %>
    <p class="-mt-2 mb-3 text-xs text-muted"><%= note %></p>
  <% end %>
  <%= yield %>
</section>
